  1020                              <1> ; `, The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes every 16-bit
  1021                              <1> ; value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones and the low
  1022                              <1> ; ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low (XOR) before the
  1023                              <1> ; remainder of dividing by n is taken.
  1024                              <1> ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
  1025                              <1> ; than 1; the unchecked one leaves a 0 alone, which DIV would fault on.
